IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb2-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part X, section 105 -- QUALIFICATIONS OF
-- DIRECTORS: who is disqualified, whether a director must hold shares, and how many directors must be
-- resident Canadians. Layer 1.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Named `<what it works out> within s <section>`. Where a provision says what follows in
-- a stated case, the rule is TRUE when that case holds; FALSE means only that this provision does not apply.
-- A rule whose result is a MAYBE returns NOTHING where the text is silent for the case.
-- Within this module a rule that depends on a sibling calls it and takes its inputs, except that a
-- classification of the corporation ("a corporation referred to in s 105(3.1)", "a holding corporation to
-- which s 105(4) applies") is passed in as its result, as the other modules pass defined terms: the rules
-- `a corporation is referred to in s 105(3.1)` and `the exception applies within s 105(4)` work it out.
-- "Prescribed" facts are plain inputs (the regulations are not among the sources).

§ `s 105 Qualifications of directors`

§§ `s 105(1) Qualifications of directors`

-- src:1228 | Qualifications of directors
-- src:1229 | 105 (1) The following persons are disqualified from being a director of a corporation:
-- src:1230 | (a) anyone who is less than eighteen years of age;
-- src:1231 | (b) anyone who is incapable;
-- src:1232 | (c) a person who is not an individual; or
-- src:1233 | (d) a person who has the status of bankrupt.
@ref CBCA s 105(1) (src:1228-1233)
GIVEN `the age of the person in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the person is incapable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has the status of bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is disqualified from being a director within s 105(1)` MEANS
        `the age of the person in years` LESS THAN 18
    OR  `the person is incapable`
    OR  (NOT `the person is an individual`)
    OR  `the person has the status of bankrupt`

§§ `s 105(2) Further qualifications`

-- src:1234 | Further qualifications
-- src:1235 | (2) Unless the articles otherwise provide, a director of a corporation is not required to hold shares issued by the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 105(2) (src:1234-1235)
GIVEN `the articles provide that a director must hold shares issued by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a director is required to hold shares within s 105(2)` MEANS
    `the articles provide that a director must hold shares issued by the corporation`

§§ `s 105(3.1) Exception -- Canadian ownership or control`

-- Any one of three circumstances. "Prescribed business sector" is a plain input.
-- src:1238 | Exception — Canadian ownership or control
-- src:1239 | (3.1) If a corporation engages in an activity in Canada in a prescribed business sector or if a corporation, by an Act of Parliament or by a regulation made under an Act of Parliament, is required, either individually or in order to engage in an activity in Canada in a particular business sector, to attain or maintain a specified level of Canadian ownership or control, or to restrict, or to comply with a restriction in relation to, the number of voting shares that any one shareholder may hold, own or control, then a majority of the directors of the corporation must be resident Canadians.
@ref CBCA s 105(3.1) (src:1238-1239)
GIVEN `the corporation engages in an activity in Canada in a business sector prescribed by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is required by an Act of Parliament or regulation, individually or to engage in an activity in a particular business sector, to attain or maintain a specified level of Canadian ownership or control` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is required by an Act of Parliament or regulation to restrict, or to comply with a restriction in relation to, the number of voting shares that any one shareholder may hold, own or control` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a corporation is referred to in s 105(3.1)` MEANS
        `the corporation engages in an activity in Canada in a business sector prescribed by the regulations`
    OR  `the corporation is required by an Act of Parliament or regulation, individually or to engage in an activity in a particular business sector, to attain or maintain a specified level of Canadian ownership or control`
    OR  `the corporation is required by an Act of Parliament or regulation to restrict, or to comply with a restriction in relation to, the number of voting shares that any one shareholder may hold, own or control`

§§ `s 105(4) Exception for holding corporation`

-- Less than five per cent of the gross revenues of the holding corporation and all its subsidiary bodies
-- corporate together is earned in Canada, directly or through the subsidiaries, as shown in the most recent
-- consolidated financial statements referred to in section 157 (out of range: section 157 (piece cb3)) or in the
-- most recent financial statements as at the end of the last completed financial year.
-- src:1244 | Exception for holding corporation
-- src:1245 | (4) Despite subsection (3.1), not more than one third of the directors of a holding corporation referred to in that subsection need be resident Canadians if the holding corporation earns in Canada directly or through its subsidiaries less than five per cent of the gross revenues of the holding corporation and all of its subsidiary bodies corporate together as shown in
-- src:1246 | (a) the most recent consolidated financial statements of the holding corporation referred to in section 157; or
-- src:1247 | (b) the most recent financial statements of the holding corporation and its subsidiary bodies corporate as at the end of the last completed financial year of the holding corporation.
@ref CBCA s 105(4) (src:1244-1247)
GIVEN `the corporation is a holding corporation referred to in subsection 105(3.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the revenues earned in Canada directly or through its subsidiaries in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the gross revenues of the holding corporation and all its subsidiary bodies corporate together in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the figures are those shown in the financial statements described in paragraph 105(4)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the exception applies within s 105(4)` MEANS
        `the corporation is a holding corporation referred to in subsection 105(3.1)`
    AND `the figures are those shown in the financial statements described in paragraph 105(4)(a) or (b)`
    AND `the gross revenues of the holding corporation and all its subsidiary bodies corporate together in dollars` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the revenues earned in Canada directly or through its subsidiaries in dollars`
            LESS THAN (5% TIMES `the gross revenues of the holding corporation and all its subsidiary bodies corporate together in dollars`)

§§ `s 105(3) Residency`

-- The least number of resident Canadian directors the corporation must have. The ordinary rule (3): at least
-- twenty-five per cent, or at least one if there are fewer than four directors. A corporation referred to in
-- (3.1): a majority; where it has only one or two directors, one (3.3). A holding corporation under (4): not
-- more than one third need be, read as at most the whole number of directors in a third, and still at least
-- one where there are only one or two directors (3.3) (fork F-P10-2). Nothing in (3.1) reduces a number or
-- percentage required elsewhere (3.2): the greater of the two applies.
-- src:1236 | Residency
-- src:1237 | (3) Subject to subsection (3.1), at least twenty-five per cent of the directors of a corporation must be resident Canadians. However, if a corporation has less than four directors, at least one director must be a resident Canadian.
-- src:1238 | Exception — Canadian ownership or control
-- src:1239 | (3.1) If a corporation engages in an activity in Canada in a prescribed business sector or if a corporation, by an Act of Parliament or by a regulation made under an Act of Parliament, is required, either individually or in order to engage in an activity in Canada in a particular business sector, to attain or maintain a specified level of Canadian ownership or control, or to restrict, or to comply with a restriction in relation to, the number of voting shares that any one shareholder may hold, own or control, then a majority of the directors of the corporation must be resident Canadians.
-- src:1240 | Clarification
-- src:1241 | (3.2) Nothing in subsection (3.1) shall be construed as reducing any requirement for a specified number or percentage of resident Canadian directors that otherwise applies to a corporation referred to in that subsection.
-- src:1242 | If only one or two directors
-- src:1243 | (3.3) If a corporation referred to in subsection (3.1) has only one or two directors, that director or one of the two directors, as the case may be, must be a resident Canadian.
@ref CBCA s 105(3) (src:1236-1243)
GIVEN `the number of directors` IS A NUMBER
      `the corporation is referred to in subsection 105(3.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exception for a holding corporation applies under subsection 105(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of resident Canadian directors required by another Act or regulation, if one is specified` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the least number of resident Canadian directors required within s 105(3)` MEANS
    `the greater of` `the number required by this section` `the other requirement`
    WHERE
        `the greater of` a b MEANS IF a GREATER THAN b THEN a ELSE b
        `the number required by this section` MEANS
            IF `the corporation is referred to in subsection 105(3.1)`
            THEN (IF `the number of directors` AT MOST 2
                  THEN 1
                  ELSE (IF `the exception for a holding corporation applies under subsection 105(4)`
                        THEN FLOOR (`the number of directors` DIVIDED BY 3)
                        ELSE (FLOOR (`the number of directors` DIVIDED BY 2)) PLUS 1))
            ELSE (IF `the number of directors` LESS THAN 4
                  THEN 1
                  ELSE CEILING (25% TIMES `the number of directors`))
        `the other requirement` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the number of resident Canadian directors required by another Act or regulation, if one is specified`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
            WHEN JUST n THEN n

-- src:1236 | Residency
-- src:1237 | (3) Subject to subsection (3.1), at least twenty-five per cent of the directors of a corporation must be resident Canadians. However, if a corporation has less than four directors, at least one director must be a resident Canadian.
-- src:1238 | Exception — Canadian ownership or control
-- src:1239 | (3.1) If a corporation engages in an activity in Canada in a prescribed business sector or if a corporation, by an Act of Parliament or by a regulation made under an Act of Parliament, is required, either individually or in order to engage in an activity in Canada in a particular business sector, to attain or maintain a specified level of Canadian ownership or control, or to restrict, or to comply with a restriction in relation to, the number of voting shares that any one shareholder may hold, own or control, then a majority of the directors of the corporation must be resident Canadians.
-- src:1240 | Clarification
-- src:1241 | (3.2) Nothing in subsection (3.1) shall be construed as reducing any requirement for a specified number or percentage of resident Canadian directors that otherwise applies to a corporation referred to in that subsection.
-- src:1242 | If only one or two directors
-- src:1243 | (3.3) If a corporation referred to in subsection (3.1) has only one or two directors, that director or one of the two directors, as the case may be, must be a resident Canadian.
@ref CBCA s 105(3) (src:1236-1243)
GIVEN `the number of directors` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of the directors who are resident Canadians` IS A NUMBER
      `the corporation is referred to in subsection 105(3.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exception for a holding corporation applies under subsection 105(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of resident Canadian directors required by another Act or regulation, if one is specified` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the residency requirement is met within s 105(3)` MEANS
    `the number of the directors who are resident Canadians`
        AT LEAST (`the least number of resident Canadian directors required within s 105(3)`
                      `the number of directors`
                      `the corporation is referred to in subsection 105(3.1)`
                      `the exception for a holding corporation applies under subsection 105(4)`
                      `the number of resident Canadian directors required by another Act or regulation, if one is specified`)
